{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCVE7VpwAqDVAY87AMqiii","type":"tool_result","content":"# LLM layer and agent loop (TS)\n\n`src/llm/`.\n\n## Adapters\n\n- Adapters read no environment variable. A protocol is an entry in\n  `ADAPTERS` (`client.ts`) with a pure encoder and an\n  `AsyncIterable<SseEvent>` decoder returning a `ModelTurn`; `send` owns\n  fetch, headers (`http.ts` `requestHeaders`), capture, usage, and\n  abort.\n- One `errors.ts`: `LlmError.kind` (underscore names, read by\n  `src/cli/errors.ts`) and `sentinels` (hyphen names, `hasSentinel`)\n  must stay in step.\n- Tool results sent to models go through `encodeToolResult` (`json.ts`)\n  only.\n\n## Agent loop (`agent.ts`, `runConversation`)\n\n- `createClient(modelClient, {ledger, now, sleep, sessionId})`\n  (`client.ts`) wraps a `ModelClient` into the finder/verifier `Client`.\n  The pure decision is `reviewResponse` (`review.ts`); the deadline,\n  ledger, final-argument validation, and retries are separate modules.\n- `ModelClient.send` owns the request timeout; the loop composes only\n  caller + deadline/window signals.\n- Cutoff errors come from `cutoffError` (`errors.ts`), which keeps the\n  cause out of the matchable chain; tests assert `details.stopCause`\n  kinds, never message text.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test/helpers/inference-server.ts` (`startInferenceServer`: a script\n  picks a reply per request; it records method, path, headers, raw and\n  parsed body) and `inference-stream.ts` (`writeInferenceStream`, the\n  native SSE per protocol).\n- Byte-level body behavior (read-ahead, caps, cancel counts) is tested\n  with a `highWaterMark: 0` `ReadableStream` returned through\n  `ClientConfig.fetch`; `new Response(stream)` neither copies nor\n  pre-reads it.\n- Agent-loop tests drive `harness(script)` from\n  `test/llm/agent-helpers.ts` (a scripted fake `ModelClient`: canned\n  turns, errors, or functions of the request; sleeps recorded).\n- `AbortSignal.timeout` timers do not keep Node alive, so a fake step\n  that waits for an abort must hold a timer (the `aborted()` helper\n  does); otherwise the test process just exits.\n# TypeScript rewrite\n\nApplies to `src/`, `test/`, and `scripts/`. Notes for one area are in\nthat area's file (index in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Tooling\n\n- `npm test` runs `typecheck`, then bundles and runs the tapzero suite.\n  A new test module must be imported from `test/index.ts`. esbuild drops\n  unused imports without resolving them, so only `typecheck` catches a\n  broken import.\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n  to `test/one-bundle.js` and runs it through tap-spec. Test modules\n  cannot run directly under Node: their `.js` import specifiers only\n  resolve once bundled. It does not typecheck; run `typecheck` too.\n- Lint with `npm run lint`: it preloads `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`, which\n  gives eslint the TypeScript 6 API because typescript-eslint throws on\n  the TypeScript 7 that `typecheck` uses.\n- Legacy launcher and release files are excluded by name from lint (the\n  `--ignore-pattern` list) and typecheck (`tsconfig.json` `exclude`);\n  the launcher compiles with `tsconfig.launcher.json`.\n- Node runs `scripts/` directly (type stripping), so they use only\n  erasable syntax: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.\n- `baseOptions` in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` holds the esbuild\n  options every bundle shares (text loaders for `.tmpl`, `.md`, `.sh`;\n  `mainFields: ['module', 'main']`, which `jsonc-parser`'s UMD build\n  needs); `scripts/bundle.ts` adds the `require` shim banner. A test\n  that bundles code itself uses both.\n- `npm run bundle` also writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (`scripts/licenses.ts`) and fails, naming the package, when a bundled\n  package lacks an allowlisted `license` field or a license file. A new\n  runtime dependency must pass it; extending `ALLOWED_LICENSES` needs\n  maintainer approval. `@substrate-system/debug` fails it today, so no\n  `src/` module may import it yet.\n\n## Source conventions\n\n- Keep source ASCII: write `\\uXXXX` escapes. Some editing tools decode\n  escapes into literal characters when writing; check with\n  `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` after writing a file. eslint `--fix`\n  (quote-props) rewrites a quoted `'\\u00e9'` object key into a literal\n  non-ASCII identifier; put such keys in a const and use a computed key.\n- eslint rejects control characters in regex literals\n  (`no-control-regex`) and labeled statements (`no-labels`); scan char\n  codes and use helper functions instead.\n- Startup guards live in `src/startup.ts`, not `src/cli.ts`: importing\n  the entry runs the CLI, so testable helpers sit in other modules.\n- Module-level swappable functions use a mutable hooks object plus a\n  delegating export (`terminalHooks`, `skillHooks.lookPath`), because\n  tests cannot reassign an ESM `let` export. Swap the object's field\n  and restore it in `t.cleanup`.\n- Shared helpers; import these, never re-implement:\n  `src/gocompat/` (`strings.ts`: Go TrimSpace/Ext/`%.2f`/strconv.Quote/\n  byte-order sort and `truncateUtf8`; `duration.ts`: Go durations as\n  bigint nanoseconds; `match.ts`: Go `path.Match`),\n  `src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`, `src/fsutil/atomic.ts`\n  (`writeFileAtomic`, options cover trust, credentials, and gate temp\n  names and error messages), `src/git/git.ts` (the only git runner;\n  pass the CLI context's `env`, it reads `process.env` only when none is\n  given), `src/util/pool.ts` (`mapPool`).\n\n## CLI core (`src/cli/`)\n\n- Commands are `CommandDef`s (`command.ts`) listed in `commands.ts`;\n  `run.ts` builds the yargs tree from that list plus `registerCommand`\n  (tests), and calls the handler only after parsing succeeds.\n- A handler gets a `RunContext` (cwd, env, signal, fetch, one shared\n  `LineReader`) and throws `UsageError` / `ExitSignal` / any error; it\n  never writes the error itself or reads process globals.\n- A group with `subcommands` and no handler prints its help.\n- yargs number parsing is off (`parse-numbers: false`). Declare an\n  integer flag as `type:'string'` and parse decimal digits in the\n  handler, throwing `UsageError` on a bad value (see `parseLimit` in\n  `runs.ts`).\n- Terminal detection and browser opening are swapped through\n  `terminalHooks` (`terminal.ts`).\n- With only the default `$0` command registered, yargs omits the\n  Commands section from root help; it appears once a second command\n  registers.\n\n## Review command (`src/cli/review.ts`)\n\n- End-to-end review tests use `settingsRepo` (`test/helpers/review.ts`):\n  a temp repo with an uncommitted change, a config on a fake `chat`\n  server, keys in env, `review.snapshot: false`, and approval via\n  `roast trust --yes`. It chdirs into the repo.\n- yargs keeps only the last occurrence of an array flag under\n  `duplicate-arguments-array: false`; review slice flags are re-read\n  from `ctx.argv` (`review-flags.ts`). Flags whose \"changed\" state\n  matters have no yargs default (`undefined` = not given).\n- The structured finder call offers `findings` plus the agent's\n  `__roast_continue`; assert tool presence, not exact lists.\n- Verification (step 17) runs only with `doVerify` and at least one\n  finding. `verify` (`src/verify/verify.ts`) never throws; an abort\n  becomes undecided verdicts, so the run still writes its record and\n  exits 4. Its result types `notes` as `string[]|null` (Go parity), so\n  CLI code after step 17 takes `VerifiedResult`, not `Result`.\n- Verifier CLI tests (`test/cli/review-verify.ts`) put the verifier on\n  its own profile and model and tell its requests apart by the\n  `submit_verdict` tool. The default role key variable\n  (`ROAST_VERIFIER_API_KEY`) backs any profile, so an invalid-key test\n  must delete it from the env.\n- The entry exits within the tick of the first SIGINT, and identical\n  signals sent back to back coalesce, so a second-signal test needs a\n  slow wind-down (a fake `git` that exits slowly on SIGTERM).\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use the `test` wrapper in `test/helpers/test.ts`, which adds Go-style\n  `t.cleanup` (tapzero has no teardown hook). tapzero's `Test` has no\n  `notOk`; write `t.ok(!x, ...)`.\n- CLI tests run in-process with `runRoast` (`test/helpers/run.ts`),\n  which makes a temp repo with an isolated env (`test/helpers/repo.ts`:\n  `tempRepo`, `tempDir`, which also sets `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES`).\n  `test/cli/process.ts` spawns `dist/cli.js`, so it needs a fresh\n  `npm run bundle` (`npm test` does that).\n- Swap terminals and the browser with `simulateTerminals` /\n  `captureBrowser` (`test/helpers/terminal.ts`).\n- Tests that spawn processes use `test/helpers/spawn.ts` (`ROOT`,\n  `run`).\n- Git runner tests observe a child by putting a fake `git` shell script\n  first on the injected `PATH` (spawn resolves the command through\n  `env.PATH`); see `test/git/git.ts`.\n- Live tests live under `test/live/` (entry `index.ts`,\n  `npm run test:live`); each passes with a \"skipped\" note when its\n  `ROAST_LIVE_*` key is unset, so the TAP stream is never empty.\n\n## Differential harness (`test/diff/`, deleted at M6)\n\n- `npm run test:diff` runs the harness self-tests (no Go needed), then\n  every scenario against the Go baseline built at `cd08f10` into\n  `node_modules/.cache/roast-diff/` (delete it to force a rebuild).\n  Without `go` on `PATH` every scenario is a TAP skip.\n- Add a milestone's scenarios as a `Scenario[]` under\n  `test/diff/scenarios/` and list it in `SCENARIOS` (`index.ts`);\n  `server`, `records`, and `requests` turn on the fake server and\n  record/request comparison.\n- A difference caused by a deliberate change goes in `ALLOWLIST`\n  (`allowlist.ts`) naming the change number. Go behavior judged wrong\n  goes in the owning area's Open questions, never patched in the\n  harness.\n- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer` (`replies.ts`),\n  keyed by `<model>#<turns>` like the request groups. A first finder\n  call has 3 messages, a first verifier call 2; an unscripted key gets\n  a 404 naming it. Credential variables must not start with a scrubbed\n  prefix (`ROAST_`, `OPENAI_`, ...): `scrubbedEnv` drops them.\n- Go-only incidental bytes are normalized, not allowlisted: SDK headers\n  (`X-Stainless-*`), Go's `\\u003c` HTML escaping (records compare as\n  parsed JSON, including `provider-responses.jsonl`), gzip/zstd bytes\n  and the bundle-manifest hashes of compressed members, finding UUIDs\n  and aliases, and the snapshot `commit` / `ref` OIDs.\n- Self-tests that need a one-sided difference wrap the TS CLI: a node\n  script that edits records after `dist/cli.js` exits, or `node\n  --import <hook>` replacing `globalThis.fetch` (the adapters send a\n  `Uint8Array` body).\nsrc/llm:\nagent.ts\ncapture.ts\nchat.ts\nclient.ts\ndeadline.ts\nerrors.ts\nfinal-args.ts\nhttp.ts\njson.ts\nledger.ts\nmessages.ts\nmodels.ts\nretry.ts\nreview.ts\nsession.ts\nsse.ts\ntypes.ts\nusage.ts\n\ntest/diff:\nallowlist.ts\nbaseline.ts\ncompare.ts\nfixture.ts\nindex.ts\nnormalize.ts\nprompts.ts\nrecords.ts\nreplies.ts\nrequests.ts\nscenario.ts\nscenarios/\nselftest/\ntar.ts\n\ntest/diff/scenarios:\nm1.ts\nm3.ts\n\ntest/helpers:\ndoctor-probe.ts\nenv.ts\ninference-server.ts\ninference-stream.ts\nprovider-server.ts\nrepo.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nspawn.ts\nstreams.ts\nterminal.ts\ntest.ts\n\ntest/live:\ndeepseek.ts\nindex.ts\n\ntest/llm:\nagent-deadline.ts\nagent-dispatch.ts\nagent-finalization.ts\nagent-helpers.ts\nagent-http.ts\ncapture.ts\nchat-decode.ts\nchat-encode.ts\nclient.ts\nerrors.ts\njson.ts\nledger.ts\nsse.ts\nusage.ts\n     572 src/llm/agent.ts\n     197 src/llm/capture.ts\n     319 src/llm/chat.ts\n     329 src/llm/client.ts\n     108 src/llm/deadline.ts\n     389 src/llm/errors.ts\n      99 src/llm/final-args.ts\n      49 src/llm/http.ts\n      43 src/llm/json.ts\n      98 src/llm/ledger.ts\n      13 src/llm/messages.ts\n      25 src/llm/models.ts\n      53 src/llm/retry.ts\n     212 src/llm/review.ts\n      24 src/llm/session.ts\n      85 src/llm/sse.ts\n     166 src/llm/types.ts\n      75 src/llm/usage.ts\n    2856 total","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce6241dd-6cf9-4ea5-b772-4d4bcdb98f32","uuid":"59784355-7bf7-409f-8ac5-c6a31ec16b28","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:46:45.487Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# LLM layer and agent loop (TS)\n\n`src/llm/`.\n\n## Adapters\n\n- Adapters read no environment variable. A protocol is an entry in\n  `ADAPTERS` (`client.ts`) with a pure encoder and an\n  `AsyncIterable<SseEvent>` decoder returning a `ModelTurn`; `send` owns\n  fetch, headers (`http.ts` `requestHeaders`), capture, usage, and\n  abort.\n- One `errors.ts`: `LlmError.kind` (underscore names, read by\n  `src/cli/errors.ts`) and `sentinels` (hyphen names, `hasSentinel`)\n  must stay in step.\n- Tool results sent to models go through `encodeToolResult` (`json.ts`)\n  only.\n\n## Agent loop (`agent.ts`, `runConversation`)\n\n- `createClient(modelClient, {ledger, now, sleep, sessionId})`\n  (`client.ts`) wraps a `ModelClient` into the finder/verifier `Client`.\n  The pure decision is `reviewResponse` (`review.ts`); the deadline,\n  ledger, final-argument validation, and retries are separate modules.\n- `ModelClient.send` owns the request timeout; the loop composes only\n  caller + deadline/window signals.\n- Cutoff errors come from `cutoffError` (`errors.ts`), which keeps the\n  cause out of the matchable chain; tests assert `details.stopCause`\n  kinds, never message text.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `test/helpers/inference-server.ts` (`startInferenceServer`: a script\n  picks a reply per request; it records method, path, headers, raw and\n  parsed body) and `inference-stream.ts` (`writeInferenceStream`, the\n  native SSE per protocol).\n- Byte-level body behavior (read-ahead, caps, cancel counts) is tested\n  with a `highWaterMark: 0` `ReadableStream` returned through\n  `ClientConfig.fetch