n `ALLOWLIST`\n  (`allowlist.ts`) naming the change number. Go behavior judged wrong\n  goes in the owning area's Open questions, never patched in the\n  harness.\n- Review scenarios script the fake with `scriptedServer` (`replies.ts`),\n  keyed by `<model>#<turns>` like the request groups. A first finder\n  call has 3 messages, a first verifier call 2; an unscripted key gets\n  a 404 naming it. Credential variables must not start with a scrubbed\n  prefix (`ROAST_`, `OPENAI_`, ...): `scrubbedEnv` drops them.\n- Go-only incidental bytes are normalized, not allowlisted: SDK headers\n  (`X-Stainless-*`), Go's `\\u003c` HTML escaping (records compare as\n  parsed JSON, including `provider-responses.jsonl`), gzip/zstd bytes\n  and the bundle-manifest hashes of compressed members, finding UUIDs\n  and aliases, and the snapshot `commit` / `ref` OIDs.\n- Self-tests that need a one-sided difference wrap the TS CLI: a node\n  script that edits records after `dist/cli.js` exits, or `node\n  --import <hook>` replacing `globalThis.fetch` (the adapters send a\n  `Uint8Array` body).\nsrc/llm:\nagent.ts\ncapture.ts\nchat.ts\nclient.ts\ndeadline.ts\nerrors.ts\nfinal-args.ts\nhttp.ts\njson.ts\nledger.ts\nmessages.ts\nmodels.ts\nretry.ts\nreview.ts\nsession.ts\nsse.ts\ntypes.ts\nusage.ts\n\ntest/diff:\nallowlist.ts\nbaseline.ts\ncompare.ts\nfixture.ts\nindex.ts\nnormalize.ts\nprompts.ts\nrecords.ts\nreplies.ts\nrequests.ts\nscenario.ts\nscenarios/\nselftest/\ntar.ts\n\ntest/diff/scenarios:\nm1.ts\nm3.ts\n\ntest/helpers:\ndoctor-probe.ts\nenv.ts\ninference-server.ts\ninference-stream.ts\nprovider-server.ts\nrepo.ts\nreview.ts\nrun.ts\nspawn.ts\nstreams.ts\nterminal.ts\ntest.ts\n\ntest/live:\ndeepseek.ts\nindex.ts\n\ntest/llm:\nagent-deadline.ts\nagent-dispatch.ts\nagent-finalization.ts\nagent-helpers.ts\nagent-http.ts\ncapture.ts\nchat-decode.ts\nchat-encode.ts\nclient.ts\nerrors.ts\njson.ts\nledger.ts\nsse.ts\nusage.ts\n     572 src/llm/agent.ts\n     197 src/llm/capture.ts\n     319