{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J55FQG5D8UyxxCfyquF5V3","type":"tool_result","content":"// Requests the fake inference server received, compared per (model,\n// turn count) group because finder and verifier calls may interleave\n// differently (spec 15, 2.13).\nimport type { RecordedRequest } from '../helpers/inference-server.js'\nimport { type Difference, deepDiff } from './compare.js'\nimport { type NormalizeContext, normalize } from './normalize.js'\n\n// Headers the HTTP clients add on their own (Go net/http vs undici).\nconst TRANSPORT = new Set([\n    'host',\n    'connection',\n    'content-length',\n    'transfer-encoding',\n    'accept-encoding',\n    'accept-language',\n    'sec-fetch-mode',\n])\n\n// Incidental Go SDK headers the TS adapters no longer send because raw\n// fetch replaced the SDKs (spec 06, section 4): not part of Roast's\n// request contract.\nconst SDK_HEADER = /^x-stainless-|^idempotency-key$/\n\nfunction turns (body:unknown):number {\n    if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null) return 0\n    const b = body as { messages?:unknown, input?:unknown }\n    if (Array.isArray(b.messages)) return b.messages.length\n    if (Array.isArray(b.input)) return b.input.length\n    return 0\n}\n\nfunction model (body:unknown):string {\n    if (typeof body !== 'object' || body === null) return ''\n    const m = (body as { model?:unknown }).model\n    return typeof m === 'string' ? m : ''\n}\n\nexport function groupKey (req:RecordedRequest):string {\n    return `${model(req.body)}#${turns(req.body)}`\n}\n\n// Header names, with values only for Content-Type and the auth scheme.\nfunction headerView (req:RecordedRequest):Record<string, string> {\n    const out:Record<string, string> = {}\n    for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(req.headers)) {\n        const v = Array.isArray(value) ? value.join(', ') : value ?? ''\n        if (TRANSPORT.has(name) || SDK_HEADER.test(name)) continue\n        if (name === 'accept' && v === '*/*') continue\n        if (name === 'content-type') out[name] = v\n        else if (name === 'authorization') out[name] = v.split(' ')[0]\n        else out[name] = '<present>'\n    }\n    return out\n}\n\nfunction view (req:RecordedRequest, ctx:NormalizeContext):unknown {\n    return normalize({\n        method:req.method,\n        path:req.path,\n        body:req.body === undefined ?\n            { '<raw>':req.rawBody.toString('utf8') } :\n            req.body,\n        headers:headerView(req),\n    }, ctx)\n}\n\nfunction groups (\n    reqs:RecordedRequest[],\n    ctx:NormalizeContext\n):Map<string, unknown[]> {\n    const out = new Map<string, unknown[]>()\n    for (const r of reqs) {\n        const key = groupKey(r)\n        const list = out.get(key) ?? []\n        list.push(view(r, ctx))\n        out.set(key, list)\n    }\n    for (const list of out.values()) {\n        list.sort((a, b) => {\n            const x = JSON.stringify(a)\n52:- **Nudge tool**: the synthetic tool `__roast_continue` that Roast always\n103:  caller's tools in caller order, then the nudge tool last. The set\n112:- Nudge tool definition:\n113:  - name `__roast_continue`\n125:  `additionalProperties: false`), plus the nudge tool. It runs with\n138:  reorders model output. Synthetic nudge calls (2.6) are appended\n194:  calls to dispatch (if any), which synthetic nudge calls to append, and\n200:neither a caller tool nor the nudge tool is reported to `onTurn`\n253:   - If `canRetrySubmission`: append a nudge call with ID\n267:F. Exploration phase, no calls (prose only): append a nudge call with ID\nbc972fa test: review on an anthropic profile end to end\na16af76 llm: anthropic adapter (encoder, decoder, dispatch) with binding and DeepSeek fakes\n983f518 redeye: update ticket checklists\n67b0d54 redeye: 26-harness-m3-review-scenarios.md done\nf2e98ef redeye: 24-runs-checkout-and-prune.md done\n4e2ee7d docs: harness review-scenario notes; spec 07 open question on the nudge