{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F67B8AqWkm82wUqUJi6hiw","type":"tool_result","content":"1194:## 8. Open questions\n1195-\n1196-1. **The nudge tool is never sent by Go.** 2.3 says every request offers\n1197-   the caller's tools plus `__roast_continue`, and `completeStructured`\n1198-   sends its schema tool plus the nudge. At `cd08f10` the Go loop does\n1199-   register the nudge with fantasy (`internal/llm/agent.go`,\n1200-   `nudgeFantasyTool`), but `prepareStep` returns `ActiveTools:\n1201-   s.active`, and `s.active` holds only the caller's tools, so fantasy\n1202-   never puts the nudge in a request. Go's `provider_test.go` asserts a\n1203-   structured request carries exactly one tool. The TS loop sends it in\n1204-   every request (`tools[last]`), so every M3 differential scenario\n1205-   (ticket 26) differs at `requests[<model>#<turns>][i].body.tools[n]`.\n1206-   This is not one of spec.md's deliberate changes, so the harness does\n1207-   not allowlist it. Decide whether TS drops the nudge from requests\n1208-   (Go parity; synthetic nudge calls in the transcript would then name a\n1209-   tool the request does not offer, as in Go) or whether sending it\n1210-   becomes a numbered deliberate change that the harness can cite.\n43:    \"test:diff\": \"npm run bundle && node scripts/bundle.ts --diff && node test/diff-bundle.js\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce6241dd-6cf9-4ea5-b772-4d4bcdb98f32","uuid":"e053d9e9-f0d6-4a42-b0d7-bf5edde2d892","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:58:38.625Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1194:## 8. Open questions\n1195-\n1196-1. **The nudge tool is never sent by Go.** 2.3 says every request offers\n1197-   the caller's tools plus `__roast_continue`, and `completeStructured`\n1198-   sends its schema tool plus the nudge. At `cd08f10` the Go loop does\n1199-   register the nudge with fantasy (`internal/llm/agent.go`,\n1200-   `nudgeFantasyTool`), but `prepareStep` returns `ActiveTools:\n1201-   s.active`, and `s.active` holds only the caller's tools, so fantasy\n1202-   never puts the nudge in a request. Go's `provider_test.go` asserts a\n1203-   structured request carries exactly one tool. The TS loop sends it in\n1204-   every request (`tools[last]`), so every M3 differential scenario\n1205-   (ticket 26) differs at `requests[<model>#<turns>][i].body.tools[n]`.\n1206-   This is not one of spec.md's deliberate changes, so the harness does\n1207-   not allowlist it. Decide whether TS drops the nudge from requests\n1208-   (Go parity; synthetic nudge calls in the transcript would then name a\n1209-   tool the request does not offer, as in Go) or whether sending it\n1210-   becomes a numbered deliberate change that the harness can cite.\n43:    \"test:diff\": \"npm run bundle && node scripts/bundle.ts --diff && node test/diff-bundle.js\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F67B8AqWkm82wUqUJi6hiw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
