`npm run lint` and `npm run test:go`. All acceptance items are done except the differential harness one: every M3 and M4 harness scenario still fails on the problem ticket 26 left open.\n\n**What was built:**\n- **The adapter** (`src/llm/anthropic.ts`): request encoding, thinking-block replay, stream decoding and finish mapping all follow spec 2.6.3 and 2.8.3. It's wired into `client.ts`; the `X-Api-Key` and `Anthropic-Version` headers were already there.\n- **Test fakes**: an `anthropic` mode for `writeInferenceStream`, plus ports of Go's binding server (rejects a changed signed-thinking prefix) and DeepSeek thinking-mode server in `test/helpers/anthropic-fakes.ts`. I checked the binding fake catches a bad replay: changing one thinking block's text makes it reject the request.\n- **CLI tests** (`test/cli/review-anthropic.ts`): one test per acceptance item. Usage comes out as 20/6/4/8/2 in `meta.json`, and an interrupted stream is retried without its partial tool running.\n- **Client-level tests**: ambient `ANTHROPIC_*` variables are ignored, a 3xx is refused without passing the key on, signed thinking replays to the binding fake in five conversation shapes, and the DeepSeek fake sees no rejected request in six modes on both `chat` and `anthropic`.\n- **Live test**: `test/live/anthropic.ts`. It skips when `ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is unset; I checked the skip but didn't run it against the real API.\n\n**Changes beyond the ticket text:**\n- `tool_choice` is `{type: \"auto\", disable_parallel_tool_use: false}`, not just `{type: \"auto\"}`. The harness showed Go sends the extra field, and the example in spec 2.6.3 includes it.\n- Two existing doctor tests assumed `anthropic` had no adapter. The doctor probe fake now speaks `anthropic`, and one assertion now checks that every request went to the verifier's host and key, since doctor now also sends an inference request there.\n\n**Harness (not checked off):** I added the M4 scenarios (`test/diff/scenarios/m4.ts`, the M3 cases on an `anthropic` profile) and an allowlist entry for deliberate change 21. Every scenario, old and new, still fails on one difference: TS offers the `__roast_continue` nudge tool in every request and Go never does. That's the open question in spec 07 section 8. Leaving the nudge aside, the M4 runs agree with Go on exit codes, JSON stdout, requests and run records. You need to decide either to drop the nudge from requests or to make it a numbered deliberate change the harness can allowlist.\n\nThe interrupted-stream CLI test takes about 5 seconds, because an incomplete stream has no retry header and falls back to the 5 s backoff.\n\n[x] A review on an `anthropic` profile against the fake posts to `<base>/v1/messages` (also when the base URL ends in `/v1`). It sends `X-Api-Key`, a non-empty `Anthropic-Version`, and no `Authorization` header. It sends `system` and `stream: true`, and the same tools on the wrap-up turn. The second request carries the injected notice. The review exits 0 or 1 by findings as with `chat`.\n[x] `max_tokens` equals the profile's `max_output_tokens` for 1024 and for 32768.\n[x] `tool_choice.type` is `auto` for converse and for structured calls, in every phase. A DeepSeek-style fake that answers 400 to any forced choice or missing `thinking` replay sees no rejected request.\n[x] Each tool's `input_schema` deep-equals the caller's full JSON Schema, including `additionalProperties` and nested `required`. `required` is `[]` when the schema has none.\n[x] A model ID containing `claude-mythos-preview` gets the adaptive `thinking` field. Other IDs send no `thinking` field.\n[x] A signed thinking block, including one that arrived after a tool call, is replayed unchanged in order. A binding fake that rejects any changed prefix accepts the follow-up request.\n[x] A 401 maps to the auth category: exit 3, and `--error-format json` reports category `auth`.\n[x] A 3xx is not followed, the redirect target never sees `x-api-key`, and the error is an endpoint error that is not retried.\n[x] Finish mapping: `end_turn` / `pause_turn` / `stop_sequence` -> `stop`; `max_tokens` / `model_context_window_exceeded` -> `length`; `refusal` / `content_filtered` / `guardrail_intervened` -> `content-filter`; other -> `unknown` with the raw reason exposed.\n[x] An interrupted stream (tool input and `stop_reason` but no `message_stop`) is retried and its partial tool never runs. All streams appear in `provider-responses.jsonl`, and `meta.json` usage counts only completed calls.\n[x] Usage accumulation over the Go fixture yields 20 / 6 / 4 / 8 / 2 (uncached, cached, cache write, output, calls) in `meta.json`.\n[x] Ambient `ANTHROPIC_*` variables (API key, auth token, base URL, custom headers) never change the endpoint, the headers, or the credential of a request.\n[x] An opt-in live test in `test/live/` (run by `npm run test:live`, never in CI): with `ROAST_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (and optional `_BASE_URL`, `_MODELS`) set, a two-turn review completes for each listed model (successor of `TestLiveAnthropicTwoTurnReview`). Without the variables it skips.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nEverything is committed in four commits. Notes for the next attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed, and reusable notes went into `docs/agents/llm.md` and `docs/agents/typescript.md`.","ttft_ms":2737,"type":"result","duration_ms":1671804,"uuid":"89555c67-18c5-4647-a02f-620c4d9d6998","ttft_stream_ms":2456,"time_to_request_ms":725,"first_content_frame_ms":2457,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":172,"outputTokens":62744,"cacheReadInputTokens":13230049,"cacheCreationInputTokens":203986,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":5.533465799999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":12077,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":2